Hello all,

I would really like to make a bar graph, but using stacks of symbols instead of bars. I was hoping geom_dotplot(), would do what I wanted, but it will only give me a plot with counts of observations rather than a plot of the values of a variable at those observations.

So I want to turn a plot like this:
library(ggplot2)
fish2 = data.frame(habitat = c("mudflat", "channel", "marsh"), catch = c(3,2,6))
ggplot(fish2, aes(x=habitat, y= catch)) + geom_bar(stat = "identity") + ylab("number of fish")

Into this (done crappily using power point):

​I know its cheesy, but it would be fun for a presentation I'm giving. I feel like there should be a way of doing it.

--
